  message: "Done in PR #3483. Bridge/FFI subset of ADR-0023 §6 Phase 3 complete. 16 production emit sites across 8 linkers (cgo, lua_ffi, pyffi, ruby_ffi, napi, wasm_bindgen×2, jni, ipc) folded to canonical 'calls' + meta['bridge_kind']; wasm_load folded to 'imports' (file→wasm_module is import-shaped, not a call). New BRIDGE_KINDS frozenset in hypergumbo_core.edge_types: closed enumeration of cgo/ffi/napi/wasm/native/context_bridge — choice of closed (vs free-form) matches ADR-0015's access_mode pattern. Consumer-side updates in scripts/bakeoff-deep (switched _FFI_EDGE_TYPES set membership to canonical-relationship + meta query) and tests/test_ipc_linker.py (18 filters rewritten). 2468 tests passing, 100% coverage on all 9 changed source files. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: centrality/slice/sketch implications of bridges-being-calls should be confirmed by a DEEP cycle on FFI-polyglot repos. Out-of-scope per Phase 4 (WI-vomoj-suhaz): io_boundary._TRACEABLE_EDGE_TYPES and taint.TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES still enumerate the deprecated bridge values (dead-but-harmless because both already include 'calls'); test_io_boundary fixtures still use old bridge names (the deprecated entries remain in _TRACEABLE_EDGE_TYPES so synthetic edges still trace)."  # 493a
